{"text": "Chaump, Joe\n\nChaikin, Karen\n\u2018Thursday, May 15, 2003 12:27 PM\n\u2018Yeager, James E.; Munoz, Fran\nFalk, David E,; Ayling, Pele; Vargas, Cesar (ALCS-SGA); Chaump, Joe\nNV UCSPP - Update\n\nFran/James,\n\nAt the end of April, we sent you notification that we took action against the enclosed list of retailers\nunder our Underage Cigareite Sales Prevention Policy. We have since come to understand that our\nwritten policy did not clearly reflect our intention, which is to take action against a retailer even though\nthe clerk, and not the retailer, may be the one that is fined or convicted by the state for the illegal sale\nof cigarettes to a minor.\n\nBecause Nevada conviets the clerk and not the retailer, in recognition that our policy was not clear to\nall retailers, we will reinstate merchandising benefits for all of the stores on the enclosed list. In other\nwords, these stores will not be under UCSPP suspension for the month of June.\n\nHowever, we are in the process of clarifying our written policy and will send it to all workload\naccounts soon. At that time, we will resume collecting information from Nevada regarding\nconvictions of clerks that occur after the clarified policy is issued, and implementing our\nUCSP Policy accordingly.\n\nPlease ensure that your Section is aware of this and that TSMs have a discussion with the affected\nretailers.\n\n1am sorry for the inconvenience.\n\nIfyou have any questions, let me know.\n\niva Checkst.doc\n78)\n\nKaren Chaikin\nTrade & Business Compliance\n\nSr68zz100eWe",
